WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Welcome back. So there you have it. That's goal setting. That's our first look at it.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
We looked at the 90-day goals. We looked at the top five goals. It's important to know when going through this.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
The first time I'm going through this, just get it done. Doesn't have to be perfect.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Because every 90 days we review how we're doing with these goals. We check them out. We see, okay, we're doing well here.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
We're struggling a bit here. And it helps us have what we call a gap analysis.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Where we can see, okay, what we forecast, where we want to go, and what do we actually achieve.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.000
And that helps us gauge where we can improve at the end of the day.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:45.000
So when I used to go with my clients doing this, it would be every 90 days we do a 90-day goal review.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:53.000
And we'll be looking at that coming up in the future. And when we do that review, we're going to unpack it systematically.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Okay, how we're doing and so forth. And we make little adjustments in calibration.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:03.000
It was the famous boxer, Floyd Mayweather, who said, okay, you may hit harder than me.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:09.000
You may be faster than me, but nobody calibrates better than me. And that was his claim to fame.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:16.000
That's why he believed he was such a world champion boxer. Because he's always making microcalibrations and adjustments.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.000
Well, it's exactly the same thing when we're doing our goal setting.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:25.000
We come back after the 90 days, we check out how we're going, same with the weekly goals, the top five.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.000
We see how we're doing, we make calibrations, and then we improve and we grow from there.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:34.000
So enjoy, and I'll see you in the next session. Ciao.